<ContentPage title="Startup Incubator" subtitle="Launch ventures that serve the community and the world.">
  <p>
    The Incubator helps turn ideas into viable businesses — ventures that generate revenue for the community
    while solving real problems. Not a Silicon Valley clone. A launchpad for enterprises that make sense
    in the context of a resilient, locally-integrated community.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Incubate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Appropriate tech ventures</strong> — products and services born from the Techno Park's R&D</li>
    <li><strong>Local-global bridges</strong> — businesses connecting Yungas resources and talent to global markets</li>
    <li><strong>Digital services</strong> — remote-work-friendly businesses that bring global income to the local economy</li>
    <li><strong>Social enterprises</strong> — ventures prioritizing community impact alongside financial sustainability</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Provide</h2>
  <p>
    Shared workspace, mentorship from experienced founders, access to the Techno Park's facilities,
    connection to the Trading House for market access, and a community of peers building alongside you.
    No equity grab — the goal is a thriving ecosystem, not a portfolio.
  </p>

  <h2>Open Knowledge</h2>
  <p>
    Business models, market research, and operational learnings are shared within the community.
    Proprietary IP belongs to founders, but the meta-knowledge — how to start a business in Bolivia,
    how to navigate export regulations, what worked and what didn't — is community commons.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-12 p-6 bg-bark-sand rounded-xl border border-bark-green/10">
    <p class="text-bark-green font-semibold mb-2">Founders and entrepreneurs</p>
    <p>Bring your idea or your experience. <a href="/en/participate">Get involved</a>.</p>
  </div>
</ContentPage>
